  - name: "Teleportation: Self"
    description: "10 P.P.E., and like every teleport channel it uses up two melee attacks/actions. Moves the Gateway plus up to 60 lbs (27 kg) of gear as far as 100 miles (160 km) per level, without error. Outdoors he may target a place he has never been if he has a good map or trustworthy directions, and he arrives on its edge, never inside a tree, vehicle or obstacle; he may also target anything in clear view. Arriving INSIDE a particular building, room or cave needs close familiarity: at least four earlier visits of some length each (about an hour is best). Otherwise the usual rules of magical teleportation apply. Strictly solo - with even a tiny thinking passenger aboard, the P.P.E. is lost and nothing happens. The obelisk in the Garden at Madhaven is the one destination he can always reach flawlessly."
  - name: "Teleportation: Others to a Familiar Location"
    description: "20 P.P.E., two melee actions. Sends one person per level of experience, each with up to 100 lbs (45 kg) extra, to a place the Gateway knows well, while he stays behind as the anchor (he may follow afterwards). Range 50 miles (80 km) per level; 99% success. Each person over his limit cuts success by 20% and risks lives. Everyone must be grouped and in physical contact; if that circuit breaks at the moment of casting, success falls to 01-49% and on a failure only one arrives, the rest landing 1D6x10 miles (16-96 km) around the target. A lone passenger must touch the Gateway. An unwilling subject may pull out of the circuit or save vs magic on a flat 16 or better with no save bonuses, and an unaware or unconscious one gets no bonuses either. The destination is always safe solid ground the Gateway himself has stood on many times - never midair, deep water or a volcano."
  - name: "Teleportation from the Obelisk"
