  - name: "Fire Energy Bolts"
    description: "1D6 M.D. per bolt, +1D6 at levels 4, 8 and 12, fired from the hands or eyes with a 1000 ft (305 m) range. 5 P.P.E. per blast; another 10 P.P.E. adds 1000 ft (305 m) more range."
  - name: "Steal & Redirect Ley Line Energy"
    description: "Blocks others from drawing ley line energy along a 20 ft (6.1 m) stretch per level: 50% chance, +3% per level. At an eclipse, solstice, ritual or similar time of power he can also divert 1D4x10% of the energy a mage summons into himself at the key moment, and cast with it. He must know who is drawing, see them, and be within 200 ft (61 m). Stolen energy keeps for five minutes per level; any excess over his normal P.P.E. capacity then dissipates harmlessly. He draws twice the normal P.P.E. at ley lines and nexus points."
  - name: "Resistance to Energy"
    description: "Half damage from lasers, ion blasts, particle beams, plasma, electricity, fire, heat and radiation. Magical energy, Ley Line Storms, Rune weapons and every kind of magic weapon hit for full damage, as do kinetic attacks - blades, clubs, bullets, arrows, Vibro-Blades, thrown objects, falls and punches."
  - name: "Bond to Cleopatra''s Needle"
    description: "Touching the obelisk transforms a trained Knight into a Gateway, granting the teleportation powers above and eight spells at reduced P.P.E. costs (book cost in brackets): D-Step [15], Dimensional Teleport [200], Distant Voice [4], Mystic Portal [30], Re-Open Gateway/Rift [50], Rift Teleportation [60], Teleport: Lesser [5], Teleport: Superior [100]. The Gateway also always senses the direction and distance to the Needle, usable as a homing compass or to fix his own position."
  - name: "A closed spell list"
    description: "The eight bonded spells are the whole of the Gateway''s spell magic. He learns no others."
  - name: "Ley Line Walker Abilities"
    description: "Senses ley lines and magic energy, and has Ley Line Phasing and Ley Line Rejuvenation, exactly as the Ley Line Walker (RUE p.113, Rifts RPG p.83)."
  - name: "Rolled O.C.C. bonus"
    description: "+1D4+3 to Spd, on top of the fixed bonuses. A rolled bonus, so it lives here rather than in bonuses."
