# Gateway Knight

## Lore

About one Knight of the White Rose in twenty can bond with Cleopatra''s Needle,
the magic-charged obelisk in the Garden. Those who do give up most of the
Mystic Knight''s energy channeling and gain teleportation in its place. They
form the Guild of Gateways: chosen for the aptitude, trained as ordinary Knights
first, then changed for good by a bonding ritual at the obelisk.

A Gateway is a trained fighter who rarely fights. The Order cannot afford to
lose one, because Gateways are how its teams leave and return to Madhaven
without leaving a trail. Every mission outside the ruins has a Gateway to send
the team out and a prearranged rendezvous to bring them back; on important
jobs, especially against the evil Mystic Knights, the Gateway stays with the
team. Their powers also suit them to spying, theft, infiltration and rescue,
and they sit on every rescue team. Knights and Squires will protect a Gateway
before anyone else, even at the cost of their own lives, which some Gateways
resent while accepting the reason for it.

## Race

No restriction. Most are human. Haven Mutants make up 2%, and D-Bees a figure
printed as ''20'' with no percent sign.

## Equipment

Beyond the kit above: 50 ft (15.2 m) of strong cord or rope and three weeks of
food rations; body armor is the standard Gateway armor, though any armor may
be worn to suit the mission. Weapons: one TW Inferno Sword, two Mutant Bone
Knives, and one weapon per W.P. with 1D6+4 spare E-Clips. Magic healing:
four White Rose petals, three White Rose leaves and two healing potions, with
more issued for special missions. Transportation is a horse in M.D.C. barding,
or with G.M. approval an exotic mount such as a Phantom Wolf or War Bird, or
else a light vehicle he can pilot or a robot horse. Besides the credits, he
starts with 2D8x1000 credits'' worth of gems and tradeable pre-Rifts artifacts.
Gateways prefer barter to spending credits, which leave a trail.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'gateway-knight');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'gateway-knight';

